#
# Counter-example for the OWL-axiom gate backing math:ProcessObservationConflation: a node
# typed BOTH math:InferenceRun (a gmeow:Activity — the process half of the process / result
# / claim separation) AND gmeow:Observation (the held claim). module.ttl asserts
# `math:InferenceRun owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation` directly, so the native DL
# reasoner forces this individual into owl:Nothing — an inconsistency the reasoned closure
# decides, not a structural heuristic. The generated `math:InferenceRun-shape` (`sh:not
# [ sh:class gmeow:Observation ]`) is the SHACL projection of the same axiom and also fires
# (shacl.NotConstraintComponent), a documented secondary gate.
# Back-reference: math:InferenceRun owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation /
# math:ProcessObservationConflation (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:conflatedRun a math:InferenceRun , gmeow:Observation .
